{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/297441-adventure-game-seeks-new-players","id":297441,"title":"Adventure! Game seeks new players.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-30T13:41:15-07:00","id":297441,"title":"Adventure! Game seeks new players.","content":"<i>Dr. Argive was a brilliant archaeologist until 1905, when he received permission to excavate on an uncharted island off the coast of Antarctica. He, along with his entire expedition, vanished. Now there are reports that ships have begun disappearing all across the southern hemisphere, and radio transmissions from Dr. Argive's old base have claimed responsibility. He demands complete surrender of all territory more than 15 degrees below the equator. </i><br /> <i>The mad scientist threatens to destroy cities, one at a time, until his demands are met. In one month, he will destroy Sydney. A month later, Capetown. A month after that, Buenos Aires. The most unbelievable part of it all? He claims he will destroy the cities with a superweapon\u2026 based on the surface of the Moon!</i><br /> <i>The year is 1922, the world is in peril, and only our heroes can save it!</i><br /> <i>....After being called to Buenos Aires by Richard Cavendish, a highly-ranked member of the Society of Adventurers, our heroes have learned that there has been mysterious activity surrounding Dr. Argive's base site. By speaking with a half-mad sailor, they also learned that mysterious &quot;monsters&quot; with tentacles have been attacking the lost ships, and the attacks seem to originate from two different locations off the Antarctic Coast. </i><br /> <i>Back at their hotel, our heroes received a message from Madam Natasha Oblavski, a world-famous clairvoyant, asking them to join her for a Message from Beyond. What will the Spirits of the Netherworld have to say? Find out, next week!</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The game takes place on Fridays, from 11 AM to 3 PM, Eastern Time. Currently, there are three players.<br /> 1) Benjamin Howard, a World-Famous archaeologist<br /> 2) James Conway, a big game hunter who happens to be a Talking Gorilla<br /> 3) Nikita Volkov, a Russian mercenary<br /> <br /> While I am using Adventure! rules, I am not using the over-arching Trinity metaplot. Magic is real, including a potential playable class (the Mystic Inspiration), and generally the world is strongly influenced by HP Lovecraft and early-era Pulp novels. It's a strange, strange world, but most well-educated people simply refuse to believe in such madness. Except those who know better.<br /> <br /> If you're interested, you can contact me on Skype as somnorianbadgermonster or via Google gmail or talk as piratezombie.<br /> The game uses Skype VoiceChat and Rolz.org.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}